    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "60cd0869_83f11dad",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/fair.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5208,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-23T19:05:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e do we have max_clamp for all background tasks?\n\nAs of now the max_clamp for background is generally left to the default value (1024), but I don\u0027t see why we couldn\u0027t change that in the appropriate rc files. As Suren suggested, this leaves userspace in control and doesn\u0027t hardcode a policy here -- other users might be happy to let the background max_clamp to 1024, and we shouldn\u0027t prevent them from doing so IMO.\n\n\u003e on older kernel with prefer_idle, this can link to prefer_idle which mapped to foreground/top_app tasks. The power efficiency probably not a top priority for upstream but for embedded system, it should be.\n\u003e that\u0027s why we disabled this boost on Pixel phones but I am considering do it for foreground/TA for benefit of UX.\n\nAgreed, this is sounds like a genuine problem and definitely wants to be addressed. The question is just about the \u0027how\u0027 we implement it.",
      "parentUuid": "bdd9c8f4_77a970c1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5208,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 5208,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "494b5dd362e728d2b9e84afb21495ae880e45972",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
